# Branch and pull request

Cut branches from updated `main`: `feat/<nn>-<slug>` (two-digit sequence, kebab-case). One concern per pull request.

Use Conventional Commits: `feat|fix|docs|test|ci|chore: <subject>` with subject at or under 72 characters.

Before opening a PR: run `git status`, review the full diff against the base branch, and read recent `git log` for message style. Run `node scripts/validate.mjs` and tests when plugin content changes.

PR summaries should cover behavior change, tests run, and risks. Use `gh pr create` when the user asks; do not open a PR unless explicitly requested.

For review feedback, use the `resolve-review-feedback` skill or `/fix`; keep the smallest safe diff.
